{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y5mprfrbwsqATUmeqQEuQ5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `quic/logger.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Public surface of the quic *text* logger backend.  Once a text\n4\t//! log file is installed on a [`Quic`] context, the context's\n5\t//! text-log slot points at the textlog implementation of\n6\t//! [`crate::logger::Logger`] and every per-event log\n7\t//! call fans out through that vtable.  The install/teardown entry\n8\t//! points hang as inherent methods on [`Quic`]\n9\t//! ([`Quic::set_textlog`] / [`Quic::textlog_close`]).\n10\t//!\n11\t//! Phase 1 contract: signatures only — every body is `todo!()`.\n12\t//!\n13\t//! Pointer-shape and translation policy notes for this module:\n14\t//!\n15\t//! * `Quic*` — every observed caller (`config.c::963`,\n16\t//!   the recursive call in `logger.c::set_textlog`) passes\n17\t//!   a non-NULL, mutable context handle.  Maps to `&mut\n18\t//!   Quic`.\n19\t//! * `char const* textlog_file` — the C contract uses `NULL` as the\n20\t//!   \"stop the text log\" sentinel, so the parameter maps to\n21\t//!   `Option<&str>`.  `Some(\"-\")` is the established\n22\t//!   redirect-to-stdout shortcut and is preserved as-is.\n23\t//! * The C return is `int` (0 on success, `-1` on file-open\n24\t//!   failure).  Mapped to `Result<(), Error>` per the project's\n25\t//!   error-handling convention.\n26\t//! * `picoquic_textlog_picotls_ticket` was the textlog backend's\n27\t//!   TLS-ticket pretty-printer.  Phase 4 reintroduces it as a\n28\t//!   private helper inside the textlog `Logger` impl; no public\n29\t//!   API needs it.\n30\t//! * `picoquic_log_fin_or_event_name` is declared in the C header\n31\t//!   but never defined or referenced — dropped from the Rust API.\n32\t\n33\tuse std::path::Path;\n34\t\n35\tuse crate::Error;\n36\tuse crate::Quic;\n37\t\n38\timpl Quic {\n39\t    /// Set the text log file and start tracing into it.\n40\t    ///\n41\t    //